WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.568
There is an alarming new development

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.303
in the already extremely tense

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.038
relationship between the United States

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:05.939
and Russia.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.741
Russia has just arrested

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.110
American journalist Evan Gershkovich

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.379
and charged him with espionage.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.714
Gershkovich is a US citizen.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.583
He has been working as a reporter

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.350
at the Wall Street

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.752
Journal's Moscow bureau.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.787
He is the first journalist U.S.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.989
journalist since 1986

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.525
who Russia has been charged with spying.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.627
CNN's Natasha Bertrand joins us now.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.062
Natasha, the Biden administration

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.563
learned about this yesterday.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.398
We're told

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.499
they only just put out

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.666
an official reaction.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.734
So what are they saying about this

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.568
arrest?

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:36.336
Yeah, Alex,

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.404
we are told that the State Department

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.238
actually learned about it

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.039
from the Wall Street

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.907
Journal who informed the administration

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.242
that their reporter

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.943
had been detained by Russian authorities.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.045
But we are getting

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.346
kind of a flurry of statements

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.447
now from the White House,

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.748
from the State Department

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.684
about the detention of this journalist,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:52.952
saying essentially

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.021
that they are deeply concerned about it,

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.389
that they have been in touch

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.991
both with his family

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.159
and also with the Wall Street

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.126
Journal on this.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.227
And also importantly,

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.195
that the State Department

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.630
has been in touch directly

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.165
with the Russian government

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.533
about his detention.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:06.933
And, of course,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.735
that is directly contradicting

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.102
something

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.270
that the Russian government had said,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.438
which is that they had received

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.139
no inquiries from the U.S. government.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.807
The US now

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.208
directly pushing back on that,

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.910
saying that they have submitted

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.777
multiple inquiries

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.112
through the consular services.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.647
They're trying to get information

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.682
on when, how and why

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.285
this reporter was detained there.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.020
Now, we also are getting

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.921
additional information

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.856
from the National Security Council

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.758
coordinator for Strategic Communications,

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:32.692
John Kirby,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.493
who told reporters

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.360
just a short time ago

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.895
that he does not know

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.764
whether this detention

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:41.067
was in retaliation for the US charging

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.268
a new operative,

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.803
a Russian spy, essentially

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:46.639
just last week for entering the U.S.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.842
illegally. And for impersonating

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.643
a foreigner, someone

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.345
he wasn't pretending to be, someone

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:52.946
he wasn't.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.814
However, it is still too early

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:55.615
at this point

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.182
to say

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.784
whether Russia is essentially trying

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:58.918
to leverage

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.620
this reporters detention

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.655
for another prisoner swap.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.490
So we'll just have to wait

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.191
and see what happens here.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:05.758
But the U.S.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.760
still trying to gather information

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.696
about why he was detained

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.498
and whether they can get any answers

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.632
on when he might be released

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.600
as of right now.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.335
He is going to be in detention

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.436
until the end of May.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.370
Alex, you know,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.271
one of the major questions

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.539
whether this was a tit for tat.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.341
Natasha Bertrand, thank you very much.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.075
This is very much

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:22.742
the beginning of

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.810
what could be a long saga.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.845
Let's continue this conversation

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.113
now with Julia Ioffe

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.114
a founding partner

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.183
and Washington correspondent for Puck,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.117
who is, I should say,

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:31.951
Russian born

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.753
and has a very deep knowledge of Russia.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.221
Julia, thank you so much

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.122
for joining me today.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.223
And I think this hits

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:40.026
particularly close to home for you and I.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.394
We met years ago

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.596
with young reporters in Moscow

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.797
like Herskovitz.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.966
And now we have these accusations

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.034
of espionage.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.303
The Kremlin saying that he was caught

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.838
red handed.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:54.274
What does Evan Jurkovich now face

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.808
with Russia's legal system?

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.777
Well, he faces

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.647
up to 20 years in a Russian penal colony.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.950
And for a young man who is 31,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.553
that is his entire youth gone,

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.655
unless obviously

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.690
some kind of deal is reached.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.592
You mentioned my background,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.427
and it's particularly relevant

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.429
in Evan's case as well.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.064
Although he was born in the U.S.,

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.832
his parents were immigrants

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:23.203
from the Soviet Union, Jewish immigrants.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.406
And there is a sense in Moscow,

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.074
especially in the foreign ministry

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.842
and in the Kremlin,

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.711
that people of this kind of background,

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.479
like my background,

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.381
they are particularly sensitive to

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:36.916
and they're particularly sensitive

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.851
to our criticism.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.421
They feel that there is a different

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.623
kind of level of betrayal

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.458
when you leave the Soviet Union,

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.594
you leave the country, you move abroad,

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.730
and you basically lob grenades at at your

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.466
homeland, at your motherland from abroad.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.936
And I think that certainly does not help

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.538
Evan's case.

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.106
Those of us who had roots

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.741
in the Soviet Union

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.943
had bigger targets on our backs,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.144
for sure.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.446
And like you,

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.480
he speaks Russian, which,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.816
of course, makes you much.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.384
Very, very strong reporters

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.353
when it comes to covering Russia.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.821
American Paul Whelan

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.488
He is, of course,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.156
still in Russian prison,

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.058
convicted on espionage charges.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:19.892
And I was speaking

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.261
with our Russian colleague,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.029
Andrei Soldatov, earlier today,

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:23.429
who told me

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.398
he thinks that Russia will start to bank,

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.733
in his words, bank

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.235
American and possibly European prisoners

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.904
for future exchanges. Do you agree?

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:33.606
Absolutely.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:33.840
And I

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.475
think they've already been doing that

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:36.876
for quite a while.

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:37.577
Unfortunately,

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.279
for the last couple of years,

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.547
and it seems they're crossing ever

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.583
brighter red lines.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:44.550
You and I both know

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:44.884
from what

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.685
we've reported there

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.120
that there are rules,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:47.820
written rules,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.121
and then

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.155
the much more important,

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.890
unwritten, unspoken rules

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:51.958
about what

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:52.692
will get you

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.793
in the most trouble

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.895
and slightly less trouble, etc.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.930
who is touchable, who isn't?

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.398
And you

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:59.165
and I both know that

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.100
when we would come back to the states

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.802
and Americans would ask us, well, aren't

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.604
you scared for your safety?

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:07.173
We both knew that it was actually

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.207
our Russian colleagues

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:08.941
who were in danger.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.109
We were protected

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.644
by our American passports.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.080
In some ways, we were untouchable

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.583
And that rule, unspoken unwritten,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.519
is now gone out the window.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.554
Like pretty much every other rule

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.121
in Russia.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:22.655
There is,

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.823
from what I understand

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.958
from speaking to people there, a sense

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.193
that anything goes

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.495
when it comes to the security services,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.630
anything goes.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.198
There are no rules.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.600
And it creates a

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.370
big sense of instability and fear.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.405
But even at a time

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:42.241
when the relationship was warmer,

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.143
like when you and I were there,

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:45.845
which is over a decade ago,

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.747
the FSB made it clear

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.082
to foreign journalists

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.416
that they were being watched.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.352
And that's something that you reported on

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:52.919
at the time.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:54.787
Yeah, they did

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:55.922
that to

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:56.756
foreign journalists,

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.924
to foreign diplomats.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:58.758
They would

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.660
break into their apartments, rearrange

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.463
the furniture, still rugs, etc.,

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.298
just to let them know

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:07.367
that they were not at home,

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.868
that they were on

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.937
somebody else's turf, their turf,

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:12.605
that they were in charge

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.974
and they were completely at their mercy

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.043
and staying in Russia at their pleasure.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.612
But it didn't result in physical harm.

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:21.681
It didn't result in arrests.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:22.448
It is

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.450
it resulted in a couple of expulsions.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.619
But that was the extent of it.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.989
This is a terrifying new low

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:32.759
and a terrifying new development.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.229
And it's frankly why

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.663
I have been scared to go to Russia

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.031
since the outbreak of the war

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.467
because of exactly this risk, because

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:42.468
you know,

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.369
everybody said, well,

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.138
but they haven't arrested

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.239
American journalists.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.074
And I would say not yet.

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:50.076
And unfortunately, here we are

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.744
and since the

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:52.378
outbreak of the war,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:54.614
we have seen many independent journalists

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:55.515
flee the country.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:57.116
Many of them are trying to keep covering

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.351
Russia and the war in Ukraine

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.285
from abroad.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.153
And it's your point.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.487
There has been protection

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.489
for international journalists

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.425
who have to be accredited.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:05.792
Many of those

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:07.059
international journalists left

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.060
and then have come back.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:08.961
So now

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.563
seeing American journalists

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.565
being arrested, charged with espionage.

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.233
What kind of chilling effect

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:15.768
do you think that's going to have

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.370
on this coverage of Russia at

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.239
what is a very, very critical time?

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:21.040
I agree with you.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:21.674
It's one of

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.409
the most important stories in the world

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.445
to be covering from inside Russia.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.814
And the fact that there is almost nobody

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:29.081
there now

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.249
makes the coverage suffer,

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.251
makes Russia more of a black box, makes

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:33.352
Russian decision

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.655
making and Russian public reaction

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:37.323
much more inscrutable.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:39.125
As you

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:40.960
said, American news organization fans

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.196
have been kind of tiptoeing back in.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:44.697
But from what I've heard

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:46.265
in light of this, news

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.334
organizations like The New York Times

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.703
are pulling people out of Russia again.

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:51.871
Because it's not safe.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:52.939
And to your earlier point

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:54.974
about banking hostages,

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.576
I've been talking to people in Moscow

00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:57.577
this morning.

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:59.011
And from what I understand, it

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.214
isn't just about a tit for tat

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.316
for this GRU officer,

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:04.550
this FSB officer

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.686
who was in prison somewhere in the west.

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:09.121
In part, it's a sense of

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.556
we no longer care

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.559
about the American reaction.

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:14.994
They think America rules the world,

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.028
including the

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:17.530
internal International Court

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.266
of Criminal Justice at at The Hague.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:24.136
And that in some ways this is payback

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.404
for the arrest warrant

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.506
that they issued

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:27.807
for Vladimir Putin,

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.342
that the gloves are off.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.878
We no longer care. It's on

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:33.746
its on with

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.681
very scary times for our colleagues

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:36.215
in Russia.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:36.782
Julia Ioffe,

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:38.484
thank you so much for joining us today

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:39.318
and for sharing your thoughts

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:41.654
really appreciate it. Thank you, Alex.

